From: SlicerWeb <slicerweb@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] BUG: Refresh the cached draw buffer when a framebuffer is bound, on ES too

vtkOpenGLState caches the draw buffer per binding point rather than per
framebuffer, and relies on re-reading it from OpenGL whenever a framebuffer is
bound to keep the cache honest. That read asks for GL_DRAW_BUFFER, which only
desktop OpenGL has, so on OpenGL ES the cache kept the previously bound
framebuffer's value and vtkglDrawBuffers skipped the call it needed to make.

A framebuffer that had been left with glDrawBuffers(GL_NONE) - which
vtkOpenGLFramebufferObject::DeactivateDrawBuffers does at the end of every use -
therefore stayed switched off the next time it was used, and everything drawn
into it, including the clear, was discarded. Volume rendering with an image
sample distance other than 1 showed this as a frozen picture: the reduced
resolution image was drawn once, when the framebuffer was new, and every later
frame kept the first one.

ES 3.0 has GL_DRAW_BUFFER0 for the same query, so use that where GL_DRAW_BUFFER
is not defined.
---
diff --git a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLState.cxx b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLState.cxx
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLState.cxx
+++ b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLState.cxx
@@ -497,6 +497,10 @@ void vtkOpenGLState::vtkglBindFramebuffer(unsigned int target, unsigned int val)
       ::glBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, val);
 #ifdef GL_DRAW_BUFFER
       ::glGetIntegerv(GL_DRAW_BUFFER, (int*)&cs.DrawBinding.DrawBuffers[0]);
+#elif defined(GL_DRAW_BUFFER0)
+      // OpenGL ES has no GL_DRAW_BUFFER. Without this the cached value would be the previously
+      // bound framebuffer's, and vtkglDrawBuffers below would skip a call it has to make.
+      ::glGetIntegerv(GL_DRAW_BUFFER0, (int*)&cs.DrawBinding.DrawBuffers[0]);
 #endif
     }
   }
